This is a project for Analysis of Algorithms 2026 at Texas Tech University. 

We will be creating an Evolutionary Agent that finds higher efficiency solutions for coding problems. 
The project will show how AI can be used to find effective weights/parameters for a given algorithm.

Quick Start
1. Follow README.md to set up the LLM api portion of the project.

2. There some additional python modules needed to use some scripts if you dont have them already
    - PySimpleGUI
    - cProfile

3. Now you can run ui.py in a command prompt and generate candidate codes in the window, choosing a number of iterations for how many you want it to generate.
    python .\ui.py

4. The candiate codes can now be evaluated with fitness.py if they are python code. See the header of the file for instructions on use.

5. Open candidate_display.html and choose a candidate result file to evaluate. The site will display its stats and then you can choose the best ones to iterate on.
    - As a baseline, we score them by the total number of function calls times the total time taken, with 0 being the perfect score.

6. Repeat until satisfied with final generation candidate.
  
